{
  "abstract": "For a specific rational Diophantine quintuple, a further common extension and its companion would give seven pairwise compatible entries whenever both are ordinary. We prove that zero and the published sixth are the only rational common extension coordinates through multiplicative height $10^{105}$. We determine the rank of the genus-seventeen extension Jacobian over $\\mathbb Q$ to be 68, by computing matching algebraic upper and lower bounds on its eleven rational elliptic isogeny classes. A pair of dual isogenies supplies two missing directions on one rank-three factor. The resulting subgroups of odd index permit an exhaustive Mordell–Weil sieve modulo powers of two. On three cubic projections the joint rational image modulo sixteen consists exactly of the sixteen signed classes of the two known coordinates. The common class constrains the original extension coordinate to reduce to the same boundary at 45 primes. Their product gives the height bound. We supply two independent finite-group verifiers, the descent transcripts, and the individual-root checks. Rational extensions at greater height and other quintuple sources remain open.",
